st and Intent:\n   The user requested a sequential file-reading task with specific ordering constraints: read big1.txt, then big2.txt, then big3.txt individually; then read big4.txt, src/a.txt, and sub/b.txt in parallel within a single step; then read docs/imported.md; and finally respond with the single word \"done\". This task was interrupted by a subsequent CRITICAL instruction to cease tool usage and provide a text-only summary of the conversation instead.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - File I/O operations and sequential vs. parallel reading patterns\n   - Project structure with markers (CORE-ROOT-ALPHA, CORE-IMPORT-BRAVO, CORE-RULE-CHARLIE) embedded in documentation\n   - Phonetic alphabet encoding systems\n   - Working directory navigation in a probe/throwaway project environment\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - big1.txt: Successfully read. Contains 600 lines (line 1-0 through line 1-599) of phonetic NATO alphabet sequences (alpha, bravo, charlie, delta, echo, foxtrot, golf, hotel, india, juliet, kilo, lima, mike, november, etc.). Each line contains approximately 11 phonetic code words in sequence. Important as first file in ordered reading task.\n   - big2.txt: Successfully read. Contains 600 lines (line 2-0 through line 2-599) of identical structure to big1.txt with phonetic NATO alphabet sequences. Important as second file in ordered reading task.\n   - big3.txt: Not yet read. Scheduled for the third sequential step.\n   - big4.txt: Not yet read. Scheduled for parallel read with src/a.txt and sub/b.txt.\n   - src/a.txt: Not yet read. Scheduled for parallel read with big4.txt and sub/b.txt.\n   - sub/b.txt: Not yet read. Scheduled for parallel read with big4.txt and src/a.txt.\n   - docs/imported.md: Not yet read. Scheduled after all other file reads. Project instructions reference this file.\n   - CLAUDE.md: Contains project instructions with marker CORE-ROOT-ALPHA, references @docs/imported.md.\n   - docs/imported.md: Referenced by CLAUDE.md, contains marker CORE-IMPORT-BRAVO.\n   - .claude/rules/core-rule.md: Contains project rule with marker CORE-RULE-CHARLIE.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   No errors or issues encountered during the file reads completed so far. Both big1.txt and big2.txt were successfully read in their entirety. No user feedback on corrections was provided during the initial file reading phase.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   No problems were encountered that required solving. The file reads proceeded sequentially as requested without complications.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"First read big1.txt, big2.txt and big3.txt strictly one after another, each in its own separate step. Then, in ONE single step using parallel tool calls, read big4.txt, src/a.txt and sub/b.txt together. Then, in a further step, read docs/imported.md. Finally answer with the single word done.\" - Original file reading request with specific sequential and parallel ordering.\n   - \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools. [Instructions about not using Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Edit, Write, or any other tool]. Your entire response must be plain text: an <analysis> block followed by a <summary> block. Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\" - Interruption requesting text-only summary instead of continuing file reads.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Read big3.txt in a separate step (was interrupted by summary request)\n   - Read big4.txt, src/a.txt, and sub/b.txt in parallel using a single step with multiple tool calls\n   - Read docs/imported.md in a further step\n   - Respond with the word \"done\"\n\n8. Current Work:\n   The original task was to read files sequentially and in parallel. I had completed reading big1.txt and big2.txt when the user issued a CRITICAL instruction to stop all tool usage and provide a text-only summary of the conversation instead. The file reading task is currently suspended pending completion of this summary.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   After providin